        "summary": "US diesel prices reached a record high of $6.53 per gallon on Sept. 21, according to the Energy Information Administration (EIA). This increase raises a freight-cost inflation risk for Bitcoin investors watching how long interest rates stay elevated. The EIA attributes the surge to tight global distillate supply and elevated crude prices. Diesel prices can contribute to higher road and rail shipping costs, depending on contracts, competition, and the duration of the fuel squeeze. A sustained rise across freight billing cycles would pose a larger inflation risk than one expensive week at the pump. If sustained fuel and freight costs keep inflation firm, the Federal Reserve could raise rates for longer, leading to a decrease in Bitcoin's value.",
        "shortSummary": "Diesel prices hit a nominal $6.53/gallop high, raising inflation concerns and potential impacts on Bitcoin, especially if sustained fuel and freight costs continue to rise.",
