        "summary": "Oil prices remain in the driver’s seat as geopolitical uncertainty continues to plague global economy. Despite a solid drop from the mid-September high, oil prices have remained the key factor in financial markets. The US dollar has seen significant gains due to Fed rate hike expectations, higher bond yields, and some safe-haven flows. The lack of restored oil and gas flows could negatively impact the global economy with winter weather conditions. Despite this, the Nasdaq 100 index and cryptocurrencies have seen solid gains. The focus will now be on key US data and Fedspeak, with key events expected to include the Conference Board Consumer Confidence index, ADP and final Q2 GDP reports, and the critical August PCE prints. The Euro is also underperformed by ECB expectations and rising oil prices.",
